  "memorial_type": "Stone of remembrance",
  "memorial_details": "Large stone (possibly limestone), vaguely triangular with finished, vertical, front face, upon which is mounted a square, polished, black marble tablet. A Bomber Command crest in gold relief is displayed above the dedication, also in gold, relief, upper-case letters.",
  "inscription": "THIS MEMORIAL IS DEDICATED TO THE SIX AIRCREW OF/ WELLINGTON BOMBER MF 116/ 26 OTU, R.A.F. WING, OXFORDSHIRE/ WHO PERISHED WHEN THEIR AIRCRAFT CRASHED/ ON THIS SPOT DURING THE NIGHT OF/ 14TH JANUARY 1945/ FG OFF N CHOBANIUK RCAF/ SGT J W MCMURDO RCAF/ SGT L G GOOD/ SGT J S GUNN/ SGT J THOMPSON/ SGT C D PARKER/ \"THEIR NAMES LIVETH FOR EVERMORE\"",
